{"abstract":"To meet their climate policy obligations towards the EU, some EU member states will have to adopt strict climate policies towards agriculture. Responding to this need, the Danish parliament recently decided to impose a tax on greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from the country's livestock production. We develop a simple model of primary agriculture and its interaction with the food industry to illustrate the main economic mechanisms determining the impact of a unilateral tax on GHG emissions from domestic agriculture. To study the allocation effects of the GHG tax on agriculture and the impact on the wider economy over time, we then present a disaggregated dynamic simulation model of Danish agriculture, embedded in a large-scale computable general equilibrium model. The model predicts that a large share of the cost increase induced by the tax will be shifted forward onto higher input prices in the food industry and ultimately onto consumers via higher food prices, but landowners will also bear a significant part of the burden through a fall in land prices. The GHG tax will induce a reallocation from animal to plant production, which would be even more pronounced in the case of a livestock-specific tax as currently foreseen, and from conventional to organic farming. This will help to reduce the total emissions from agriculture, but the largest share of the emission cuts will stem from a fall in output, as there are still few low-cost technical abatement possibilities in agriculture.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sørensen, Peter Birch","Beck, Ulrik Richardt","Berg, Asbjørn Kehlet","Christiansen, Simon","Løchte Jørgensen, Cecilie Marie","Kirk, Jens Sand","Stewart, Louis Birk","Stephensen, Peter Philip"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813569"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Peter Birch"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["KRAKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of unilateral climate policy towards agriculture a case study of denmark","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1477-9552.12624","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-813569","identifier":[{"id":"85214836729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-229d4c41-702b-47cf-8790-09bdf7c0a326","ku-b4347faa-3156-48e9-b8e8-bc99da6864e8"],"keyword":["tax on non-CO emissions","unilateral climate policy towards agriculture"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-69172607A548A9157C1371AC52D69EC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1477-9552.12624","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/454319172/J_Agricultural_Economics_-_2025_-_S_rensen_-_The_effects_of_unilateral_climate_policy_towards_agriculture_A_case_study_of.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Economics, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["KRAKA"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Economics and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter Birch","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"2ea16574-8915-4912-9787-0e69a011945d","name":"Sørensen, Peter Birch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik Richardt","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Ulrik Richardt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Asbjørn Kehlet","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Asbjørn Kehlet","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Simon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cecilie Marie","key":"løchtejørgensenpau","last":"Løchte Jørgensen","locid":"4c02c76b-e23d-4c5c-b1aa-82d8cfd3c380","name":"Løchte Jørgensen, Cecilie Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-1468-7339","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Sand","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","name":"Kirk, Jens Sand","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Louis Birk Søndergaard","key":"stewartpau","last":"Stewart","name":"Stewart, Louis Birk Søndergaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter Philip","key":"stephensenpau","last":"Stephensen","name":"Stephensen, Peter Philip","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1477-9552.12624","issn":["0021857X","14779552"],"issn_org":["0021857X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Agricultural Economics","pages":"3-23","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agricultural Economics","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214836729"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-229d4c41-702b-47cf-8790-09bdf7c0a326","ku-b4347faa-3156-48e9-b8e8-bc99da6864e8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of unilateral climate policy towards agriculture: A case study of Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-813569","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: To investigate the association between chronic inflammation and subclinical left ventricular dysfunction in type 1 diabetes (T1D). METHODS: In a cross-sectional study of individuals with T1D without known heart disease, interleukin-6 (IL-6), soluble-urokinase-plasminogen-activator-receptor (suPAR), and high-sensitivity C-reactive-protein (hsCRP) were examined for associations with echocardiographic E/e' (primary outcome) and global longitudinal strain (GLS) (secondary outcome). We adjusted for several clinical variables in linear regression analysis, including N-terminal pro-B-type natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP). The biomarkers were categorized as elevated/non-elevated based on their upper quartiles. RESULTS: Of 962 individuals (52 % male, mean age 49 ± 14 years), mean E/e' was 7 ± 3 and GLS 18 ± 3. In fully adjusted models, all biomarkers were each associated with increased E/e': beta coefficients for IL-6 0.2 (95 % confidence intervals: 0.1-0.3, P = 0.001), suPAR 0.5 (0.1-0.7, P = 0.011), and hsCRP 0.1 (0.0-0.2, P = 0.023). Combining biomarkers showed stronger associations: elevated IL-6 and suPAR 1.3 (0.7-2.0, P < 0.001), elevated all three 1.9 (1.1-2.7, P < 0.001). Results were similar for decreased GLS with IL-6--0.4 (-0.7 to 0.0, P = 0.039), IL6 and hsCRP -1.0 (-1.7 to -0.4, P = 0.007), all three -1.1 (-2.0 to -0.3, P = 0.009). CONCLUSIONS: Inflammatory biomarkers are independently associated with subclinical left ventricular dysfunction. Chronic inflammation may contribute to the development of myocardial dysfunction in T1D.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Dixen, Ulrik","Rasmussen, Line Jee Hartmann","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Rossing, Peter","Jensen, Magnus Thorsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798786"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Queen Mary University of London"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between interleukin 000000000006 supar and hscrp with subclinical left ventricular dysfunction in type 000000000001 diabetes the thousand amp 000000000001 study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2025.112071","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798786","identifier":[{"id":"40043809","type":"pmid"},{"id":"86000594772","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0113cdac-a818-4934-bf90-cad1c5aec578"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D95E99BE7B69445F691D600DAAB9F018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2025.112071","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/453635856/Association_between_interleukin-6_suPAR_and_hsCRP_with_subclinical_left_ventricular_dysfunction_in_type_1_diabetes_The_Thousand_amp_1_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Hashmat Sayed Zohori","key":"bahramipau","last":"Bahrami","name":"Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter Godsk","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Jens Dahlgaard","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Ulrik","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"7e6776f1-74ea-4184-a19e-03f6bd2e7de4","name":"Dixen, Ulrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Line Jee Hartmann","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Line Jee Hartmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 5","first":"Magnus T","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ddd14a07-41ed-4fb0-a380-9c28f9de46f7","name":"Jensen, Magnus Thorsten","name_org":"Jensen, Magnus T","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40043809"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.diabres.2025.112071","issn":["01688227","15721671"],"issn_org":["01688227"],"journal":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","paperid":"112071","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice","volume":"222"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000594772"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0113cdac-a818-4934-bf90-cad1c5aec578"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between interleukin-6, suPAR, and hsCRP with subclinical left ventricular dysfunction in type 1 diabetes : The Thousand &amp; 1 study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798786","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Type 1 diabetes (T1D) increases premature mortality risk, with cardiovascular disease being the leading cause. Chronic inflammation may play a role. Associations between inflammatory biomarkers and mortality are not well-known in T1D. Methods: We evaluated a prospective clinical cohort with T1D without known cardiovascular disease. The inflammatory biomarkers soluble-urokinase-plasminogen-activator-receptor (suPAR) and interleukin-6 (IL-6) were measured. Patients were stratified by elevated/low suPAR or IL-6, or simultaneously elevated suPAR and IL-6. Primary and secondary endpoints were all-cause mortality and major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE), respectively. Cox models were adjusted for 10 Steno T1 Risk Engine variables and inflammatory biomarkers. Net reclassification improvement (NRI) and C-statistics were calculated. Results: Among 962 participants (52% male, median age 50, median follow-up 13.1 years), mortality was higher in patients with elevated inflammation: 31% for elevated versus 9% for low suPAR; 30% for elevated versus 11% for low IL-6; and 50% for simultaneously elevated suPAR and IL-6 versus 5% for low suPAR and IL-6. In fully adjusted models, elevated inflammation was associated with mortality (hazard ratios [95% confidence intervals]: suPAR 2.0 [1.4–3.0, p < 0.001], IL-6 1.8 [1.3–2.6; p = 0.001], and combined 4.0 [2.3–7.2, p < 0.001]) and MACE (suPAR 1.9 [1.4–2.6, p < 0.001], IL-6 1.4 [1.0–1.8, p = 0.034], and combined 2.6 [1.7–4.1, p < 0.001]). Adding suPAR, IL-6, and their combination to the Steno T1 Risk Engine improved NRI for mortality by 61%, 53%, and 84%, respectively, whereas C-statistics improved from 0.808 to 0.829, 0.826, and 0.881, respectively. Conclusions: suPAR, IL-6, and especially their combination independently predicts all-cause mortality and MACE in T1D without known cardiovascular disease.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Dixen, Ulrik","Rasmussen, Line Jee Hartmann","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Rossing, Peter","Jensen, Magnus Thorsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829366"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Cardiovascular Diseases","Diabetes","Inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"soluble urokinase plasminogen activator receptor and interleukin 000000000006 improves prediction of all cause mortality and major adverse cardiovascular events in type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/joim.20108","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829366","identifier":[{"id":"40619914","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105009836516","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8d8db099-a7ca-4400-aa18-132b273e7b59"],"keyword":["biomarkers","cardiovascular diseases","diabetes","inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3792BEB0ABEC989E6DDC585E925724CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/joim.20108","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/462200388/Journal_of_Internal_Medicine_-_2025_-_Bahrami_-_Soluble_urokinase_plasminogen_activator_receptor_and_interleukin_6_improves.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Hashmat Sayed Zohori","key":"bahramipau","last":"Bahrami","name":"Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peter Godsk","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Jens Dahlgaard","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Ulrik","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"7e6776f1-74ea-4184-a19e-03f6bd2e7de4","name":"Dixen, Ulrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Line Jee Hartmann","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Line Jee Hartmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 5","first":"Magnus T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ddd14a07-41ed-4fb0-a380-9c28f9de46f7","name":"Jensen, Magnus Thorsten","name_org":"Jensen, Magnus T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40619914"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/joim.20108","issn":["09546820","09557873"],"issn_org":["09546820"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Internal Medicine","pages":"188-199","status":"p","title":"Journal of Internal Medicine","volume":"298"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009836516"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8d8db099-a7ca-4400-aa18-132b273e7b59"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Soluble urokinase plasminogen activator receptor and interleukin-6 improves prediction of all-cause mortality and major adverse cardiovascular events in Type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829366","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Vitamin K is a cofactor necessary for the biological activity of proteins like Matrix Gla Protein (MGP), which reduce calcification and help preserve lung function. This study aims to determine, first, whether low vitamin K status is associated with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), and secondary, whether the level of vitamin K is associated with COPD severity, smoking exposure, or mortality. Methods: The plasma concentration of dephosphorylated uncarboxylated (dp-uc) MGP was used as an inverse biomarker for vitamin K in 98 COPD patients from the CODEX-P COPD study and 986 controls from the DanFunD study. Low vitamin K status was defined as the upper quartile of dp-ucMGP (>589 pmol/L). Using a logistic regression model, we examined whether low vs. high/moderate vitamin K status increased the odds ratio (OR) of having COPD. Secondary analyses, in the COPD cohort only, examined the association between low vitamin K status and COPD severity, smoking exposure in packyears and all-cause mortality, using a Welch’s t-test and log-rank test, respectively. Results: Low vitamin K status was associated with increased odds of having COPD, OR 9.7 (95% CI [5.5 to 17.5], p < 0.001). We found no associations between low vitamin K and COPD severity (est. −0.03, p = 0.7; 95% CI [−0.2 to 0.1]), smoking exposure (p = 0.7), or all-cause mortality (p = 0.5). Conclusions: Low vitamin K status was associated with substantially higher odds of having COPD compared to high/moderate vitamin K status. No association was found between low vitamin K status and COPD severity, smoking exposure, or all-cause mortality. Further studies are needed to determine if vitamin K plays a role in the pathophysiology of COPD and whether supplement therapy is indicated.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Ackermann, Daniel Alexander","Linneberg, Allan","Rastoder, Ema","Vognsen, Anna Kubel","Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","Friis-Hansen, Lennart","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Hedsund, Caroline Emma","Johansen, Niklas Dyrby","Modin, Daniel","Dons, Maria","Højbjerg Lassen, Mats C.","Grundtvig Skaarup, Kristoffer","Vesterlev, Ditte","Moberg, Mia","Janner, Julie","Eklöf, Josefin","Pedersen, Lars","Bendstrup, Elisabeth","Laursen, Christian B.","Carlsen, Jørn","Biering-Sørensen, Tor","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Sivapalan, Pradeesh"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-804234"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Ackermann, Daniel Alexander","Sivapalan, Pradeesh"],"keyword":["Biomarker","COPD","Vitamin K","dp ucMGP"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low vitamin k status and risk of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines13040807","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.97-804234","identifier":[{"id":"40299372","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003578012","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12024738","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d0c44f4e-0ab0-4361-bea6-c6fb0c287400","ku-383ba3f4-663a-42f9-b1ab-6154f0687555","sdu-c5b18680-f4bd-48f3-9f05-0831bab60efe"],"keyword":["COPD","biomarker","dp-ucMGP","vitamin K"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A139EC7A3D1AF768D82815FA8DFBBD87"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines13040807","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/4489