,"name":"Modin, Daniel","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Maria","key":"donspau","last":"Dons","locid":"c9e06b39-b8c2-4b37-92b7-c4632e1a4274","name":"Dons, Maria","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mats C.","key":"højbjerglassenpau","last":"Højbjerg Lassen","locid":"3e86e08a-c881-4afc-a540-35c1933fef45","name":"Lassen, Mats Christian Højbjerg","name_org":"Højbjerg Lassen, Mats C.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kristoffer","key":"grundtvigskaaruppau","last":"Grundtvig Skaarup","name":"Grundtvig Skaarup, Kristoffer","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ditte","key":"vesterlevpau","last":"Vesterlev","name":"Vesterlev, Ditte","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia","key":"mobergpau","last":"Moberg","name":"Moberg, Mia","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie","key":"jannerpau","last":"Janner","name":"Janner, Julie","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Josefin","key":"eklöfpau","last":"Eklöf","name":"Eklöf, Josefin","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lars","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Elisabeth","key":"bendstruppau","last":"Bendstrup","locid":"be043b5b-018b-48e2-8020-9cc943355a94","name":"Bendstrup, Elisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-4238-6963","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian B","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"333fc524-a408-42f4-885a-0fee79e488b9","name":"Laursen, Christian B","orcid":"0000-0001-6382-9906","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jørn","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"d1394cd1-fa74-45ea-a5f4-7730f6c6de0c","name":"Carlsen, Jørn","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 5","first":"Tor","key":"bieringsørensenpau","last":"Biering-Sørensen","locid":"2a25298f-30d3-4b37-b20b-646684a29fd8","name":"Biering-Sørensen, Tor","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jens Ulrik Stæhr","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d9593acd-d6ae-4a83-a7c8-64bc2ea541ac","name":"Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","orcid":"0000-0003-4036-0521","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Pradeesh","key":"sivapalanpau","last":"Sivapalan","locid":"bd238e0e-9259-49fe-b6b3-fcea0c6f20cd","name":"Sivapalan, Pradeesh","orcid":"0000-0002-8620-3655","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40299372"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biomedicines13040807","issn":["22279059"],"issue":"4","journal":"Biomedicines","paperid":"807","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Biomedicines","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003578012"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d0c44f4e-0ab0-4361-bea6-c6fb0c287400","ku-383ba3f4-663a-42f9-b1ab-6154f0687555","sdu-c5b18680-f4bd-48f3-9f05-0831bab60efe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Low Vitamin K Status and Risk of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.97-804234","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Metabolic effects of empagliflozin treatment include lowered glucose and insulin concentrations, elevated free fatty acids and ketone bodies and have been suggested to contribute to the cardiovascular benefits of empagliflozin treatment, possibly through an improved cardiac function. We aimed to evaluate the influence of these metabolic changes on cardiac function in patients with T2D. Methods: In a randomized cross-over design, the SGLT2 inhibitor empagliflozin (E) was compared with insulin (I) treatment titrated to the same level of glycemic control in 17 patients with type 2 diabetes, BMI of > 28 kg/m2, C-peptide > 500 pM. Treatments lasted 5 weeks and were preceded by 3-week washouts (WO). At the end of treatments and washouts, cardiac diastolic function was determined with magnetic resonance imaging from left ventricle early peak-filling rate and left atrial passive emptying fraction (primary and key secondary endpoints); systolic function from left ventricle ejection fraction (secondary endpoint). Coupling between cardiac function and fatty acid concentrations, was studied on a separate day with a second scan after reduction of plasma fatty acids with acipimox. Data are Mean ± standard error. Between treatment difference (ΔT: E–I) and treatments effects (ΔE: E-WO or ΔI: I -WO) were evaluated using Students’ t-test or Wilcoxon signed rank test as appropriate. Results: Glucose concentrations were similar, fatty acids, ketone bodies and lipid oxidation increased while insulin concentrations decreased on empagliflozin compared with insulin treatment. Cardiac diastolic and systolic function were unchanged by either treatment. Acipimox decreased fatty acids with 35% at all visits, and this led to reduced cardiac diastolic (ΔT: −51 ± 22 ml/s (p < 0.05); ΔE: −33 ± 26 ml/s (ns); ΔI: 37 ± 26 (ns, p < 0.05 vs ΔE)) and systolic function (ΔT: -3 ± 1% (p < 0.05); ΔE: −3 ± 1% (p < 0.05): ΔI: 1 ± 2 (ns, ns vs ΔE)) under chronotropic stress during empagliflozin compared to insulin treatment. Conclusions: Despite significant metabolic differences, cardiac function did not differ on empagliflozin compared with insulin treatment. Impaired cardiac function during acipimox treatment, could suggest greater cardiac reliance on lipid metabolism for proper function during empagliflozin treatment in patients with type 2 diabetes. Trial registration: EudraCT 2017-002101-35, August 2017.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Thirumathyam, Roopameera","Richter, Erik A.","van Hall, Gerrit","Holst, Jens Juul","Fenger, Mogens","Gøtze, Jens P.","Dixen, Ulrik","Vejlstrup, Niels","Madsbad, Sten","Madsen, Per Lav","Jørgensen, Nils Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721370"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiac function","Hyperinsulinemia","Metabolism","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of empagliflozin induced metabolic changes for cardiac function in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes a randomized cross over magnetic resonance imaging study with insulin as comparator","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12933-023-02094-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721370","identifier":[{"id":"85181464935","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38184612","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10771642","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a4800d6e-df02-4e98-b760-12a772b04617"],"keyword":["Cardiac function","Hyperinsulinemia","Metabolism","Sodium-glucose linked transporter 2 inhibition","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77B4E4E077E6EF1A805A7FE124D622EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379659994/The_role_of_empaglifozin_induced.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12933-023-02094-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Molecular Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Roopameera","key":"thirumathyampau","last":"Thirumathyam","name":"Thirumathyam, Roopameera","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik Arne","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"c9ba60ad-a6b9-439f-bbd2-e6fd31a4e009","name":"Richter, Erik A.","name_org":"Richter, Erik Arne","orcid":"0000-0002-6850-3056","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Gerrit","key":"vanhallpau","last":"van Hall","locid":"55a9b111-6dbb-4a42-a9ab-d5f3785fbdae","name":"van Hall, Gerrit","orcid":"0000-0002-2519-8127","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens","key":"fengerpau","last":"Fenger","name":"Fenger, Mogens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens P.","key":"gøtzepau","last":"Gøtze","name":"Gøtze, Jens P.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ulrik","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"7e6776f1-74ea-4184-a19e-03f6bd2e7de4","name":"Dixen, Ulrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per Lav","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"267156f7-77df-4317-9a18-c34453d1f469","name":"Madsen, Per Lav","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nils Bruun","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils Bruun","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38184612"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12933-023-02094-x","issn":["14752840"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cardiovascular Diabetology","pages":"1-13","paperid":"13","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Diabetology","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181464935"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a4800d6e-df02-4e98-b760-12a772b04617"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The role of empagliflozin-induced metabolic changes for cardiac function in patients with type 2 diabetes. A randomized cross-over magnetic resonance imaging study with insulin as comparator","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721370","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Cardiovascular disease (CVD) is the leading cause of mortality and morbidity in type 1 (T1D) and type 2 diabetes (T2D). Despite diabetes affects the myocardium, risk prediction models do not include myocardial function parameters. Myocardial performance index (MPI) reflects left ventricular function. The prognostic value of MPI has not been evaluated in large-scale diabetes populations. METHODS AND RESULTS: We evaluated two prospective cohort studies: Thousand&1 (1093 individuals with T1D) and Thousand&2 (1030 individuals with T2D). Clinical data, including echocardiography, were collected at baseline. We collected follow-up data from national registries. We defined major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE) as incident events of hospital admission for acute coronary syndrome, heart failure, stroke, or all-cause mortality. For included individuals (56% male, 54 ± 15 years, MPI 0.51 ± 0.1, 63% T1D), follow-up was 100% after median of 5.3 years (range: 4.8-6.3). MPI was associated with MACE (HR 1.2, 95%CI 1.0-1.3, P = 0.012, per 0.10-unit increase) and heart failure (HR 1.3, 95%CI 1.1-1.6, P = 0.005, per 0.10-unit increase) after adjusting for clinical and echocardiographic variables. MPI predicted MACE and heart failure better in T1D than T2D (P = 0.031 for interaction). MPI added discriminatory power to the Steno T1 Risk Engine, based on clinical characteristics, in predicting MACE [area under the curve (AUC) from 0.77 to 0.79, P = 0.030] and heart failure (AUC from 0.77 to 0.83, P = 0.009) in T1D. CONCLUSION: MPI is independently associated with MACE and heart failure in T1D but not T2D and improves prediction in T1D. Echocardiographic assessment in T1D may enhance risk prediction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Dixen, Ulrik","Biering-Sørensen, Tor","Rossing, Peter","Jensen, Magnus T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702381"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 complications","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 complications","Female","Heart Failure etiology","Humans","Male","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic value of myocardial performance index in individuals with type 000000000001 and type 000000000002 diabetes thousand amp 000000000001 and thousand amp 000000000002 studies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-702381","identifier":[{"id":"85175404828","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37638773","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d5b31a5c-579c-4e0e-a1f7-e4722cc1626b"],"keyword":["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1/complications","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/complications","Female","Heart Failure/etiology","Humans","Male","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAFFC29110B40E691DC8CABA194B3A1C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Hashmat Sayed Zohori","key":"bahramipau","last":"Bahrami","name":"Bahrami, Hashmat Sayed Zohori","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Peter Godsk","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens Dahlgaard","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","locid":"4ecfb416-ea53-418e-a6c3-ace7647318ea","name":"Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5600-5623","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ulrik","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"7e6776f1-74ea-4184-a19e-03f6bd2e7de4","name":"Dixen, Ulrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tor","key":"bieringsørensenpau","last":"Biering-Sørensen","locid":"2a25298f-30d3-4b37-b20b-646684a29fd8","name":"Biering-Sørensen, Tor","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4","first":"Magnus T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Magnus T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37638773"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ehjci/jead178","issn":["15252167","15322114"],"issn_org":["20472404"],"issue":"11","journal":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","pages":"1555-1562","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal Cardiovascular Imaging","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175404828"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d5b31a5c-579c-4e0e-a1f7-e4722cc1626b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prognostic value of myocardial performance index in individuals with type 1 and type 2 diabetes : Thousand&amp;1 and Thousand&amp;2 studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-702381","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Among ICU patients with COVID-19, it is largely unknown how the overall outcome and resource use have changed with time, different genetic variants, and vaccination status. Methods For all Danish ICU patients with COVID-19 from March 10, 2020 to March 31, 2022, we manually retrieved data on demographics, comorbidities, vaccination status, use of life support, length of stay, and vital status from medical records. We compared patients based on the period of admittance and vaccination status and described changes in epidemiology related to the Omicron variant. Results Among all 2167 ICU patients with COVID-19, 327 were admitted during the first (March 10–19, 2020), 1053 during the second (May 20, 2020 to June 30, 2021) and 787 during the third wave (July 1, 2021 to March 31, 2022). We observed changes over the three waves in age (median 72 vs. 68 vs. 65 years), use of invasive mechanical ventilation (81% vs. 58% vs. 51%), renal replacement therapy (26% vs. 13% vs. 12%), extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (7% vs. 3% vs. 2%), duration of invasive mechanical ventilation (median 13 vs. 13 vs. 9 days) and ICU length of stay (median 13 vs. 10 vs. 7 days). Despite these changes, 90-day mortality remained constant (36% vs. 35% vs. 33%). Vaccination rates among ICU patients were 42% as compared to 80% in society. Unvaccinated versus vaccinated patients were younger (median 57 vs. 73 years), had less comorbidity (50% vs. 78%), and had lower 90-day mortality (29% vs. 51%). Patient characteristics changed significantly after the Omicron variant became dominant including a decrease in the use of COVID-specific pharmacological agents from 95% to 69%. Conclusions In Danish ICUs, the use of life support declined, while mortality seemed unchanged throughout the three waves of COVID-19. Vaccination rates were lower among ICU patients than in society, but the selected group of vaccinated patients admitted to the ICU still had very severe disease courses. When the Omicron variant became dominant a lower fraction of SARS-CoV-2 positive patients received COVID treatment indicating other causes for ICU admission.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Meier, Nick","Perner, Anders","Plovsing, Ronni","Christensen, Steffen","Poulsen, Lone M.","Brøchner, Anne C.","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Helleberg, Marie","Jensen, Jens U. S.","Andersen, Lars P. K.","Siegel, Hanna","Ibsen, Michael","Jørgensen, Vibeke L.","Winding, Robert","Iversen, Susanne","Pedersen, Henrik P.","Sølling, Christoffer","Garcia, Ricardo S.","Michelsen, Jens","Mohr, Thomas","Michagin, George","Espelund, Ulrick S.","Bundgaard, Helle","Kirkegaard, Lynge","Smitt, Margit","Sigurdsson, Sigurdur","Buck, David L.","Ribergaard, Niels-Erik","Pedersen, Helle S.","Toft, Mette Helene","Jonassen, Trine B.","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Madsen, Emilie K.","Haberlandt, Trine N.","Bredahl, Louise Sophie","Haase, Nicolai"],"cuid":["S04-096.25-715795"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Meier, Nick"],"keyword":["Aged","COVID 19 therapy","COVID 19 vaccination","COVID 19 variants","Covid 19","Critical care","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Intensive care unit","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term outcomes in covid 000000000019 patients admitted to intensive care in denmark a nationwide observational study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14290","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by Statens Serum Institut (SST) and Regionernes Kliniske Kvalitetsudviklingsprogram (RKKP)."],"id":"S04-096.25-715795","identifier":[{"id":"37288935","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85161547094","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dc1aa9f2-6f50-4853-83ad-28bb1d1c9220","au-7d1ff590-4fb4-45a0-9d19-615bdb53efcd","ku-4e400344-3f4a-4a48-a016-1486b7f1e790","sdu-4aef73d2-4d94-41fb-87da-3b3d33084801"],"keyword":["Aged","COVID-19","COVID-19 vaccination","COVID-19 variants","COVID-19/therapy","Critical Care","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","SARS-CoV-2","intensive care unit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-4DC8FA96ECB082584ECBA36D7BB862E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14290","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/551308934/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_-_2023_-_Meier_-_Long_term_outcomes_in_COVID_19_patients_admitted_to_intensive_care_in_Denmark_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/242364600/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/405987186/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_-_2023_-_Meier_-_Long_term_outcomes_in_COVID_19_patients_admitted_to_intensive_care_in_Denmark_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/374568522/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2023_Meier_Long_term_outcomes_in_COVID_19_patients_admitted_to_intensive_care_in_Denmark_A.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI