 Geriatric Cancer Research (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Lembrecht","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"f9eac821-ade9-44b6-8f42-747089a921cf","name":"Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","orcid":"0000-0002-7968-2694","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens-Ulrik","key":"rosholmpau","last":"Rosholm","locid":"42011e4d-4ddc-4850-bf2b-1fba8b412125","name":"Rosholm, Jens-Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0003-4730-467X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"werenbergpau","last":"Werenberg","locid":"f6bc4419-b23d-4025-968b-bfd64b64c8e3","name":"Werenberg, Helene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn","key":"herrstedtpau","last":"Herrstedt","locid":"ea88fcb8-e0ec-4439-815d-d3ead82a2a7c","name":"Herrstedt, Jørn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["23789409"],"issue":"1","journal":"Annals of Gerontology and Geriatric Research","paperid":"1055","status":"p","title":"Annals of Gerontology and Geriatric Research","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a267ef5f-2ffa-431a-93ba-16f7ab80ae4b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Potentially Inappropriate Medication and potential drug interactions with Toxicity and Adherence to Anti-Neoplastic Treatment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-619682","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Device-related infection (DRI) is a severe complication of treatment with cardiac implantable electronic devices. Identification of the causative pathogen is essential for optimal treatment, but conventional methods often are inadequate. Objective: The purpose of this study was to improve microbiological diagnosis in DRI using sonication and next-generation sequencing analysis. The primary objective was identification of causative pathogens. The secondary objective was estimation of the sensitivity of different microbiological methods in detecting the causative pathogen. Methods: Consecutive patients with clinical signs of DRI between October 2016 and January 2019 from 3 tertiary centers in Denmark were included in the study. Patients underwent a diagnostic approach, including blood cultures and perioperative collection of microbiological samples (pocket swab, pocket tissue biopsies, generator, and leads). Conventional culturing was performed, and device components were sonicated and examined with an amplicon-based metagenomic analysis using next-generation sequencing. The results were compared with a reference standard–identified causative pathogen. Results: In 110 patients with clinical signs of pocket (n = 50) or systemic DRI (n = 60), we collected 109 pocket swabs, 220 pocket tissue biopsies, 106 generators, 235 leads, and a minimum 1 set of blood cultures from 102 patients. Combining all findings, we identified the causative pathogen in 95% of cases, irrespective of DRI type. The usability of each microbiological method differed between DRI types. In pocket DRI, next-generation sequencing analysis of generators achieved sensitivity of 90%. For systemic DRI, blood cultures reached sensitivity of 93%. Conclusion: Using a strategy including sonication and next-generation sequencing, we identified the causative pathogen in 95% of DRI. Sensitivity of microbiological methods differed according to the type of DRI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Olsen, Thomas","Justesen, Ulrik Stenz","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Jørgensen, Ole Dan","Foldager Sandgaard, Niels Christian","Ravn, Christen","Gerdes, Christian","Thøgersen, Anna Margrethe","Gill, Sabine","Fuursted, Kurt","Johansen, Jens Brock"],"cuid":["S02-098.86-014039"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Olsen, Thomas"],"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device","Cardiac implantable electronic device infection","Defibrillators Implantable adverse effects","Device related infection","Electronics","Heart Diseases","High Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Infection","Molecular microbiology","Next generation sequencing","Pacemaker Artificial adverse effects","Prosthesis Related Infections diagnosis","Sonication","Sonication methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Danish Pacemaker and ICD Register"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbiological diagnosis in cardiac implantable electronic device infections detected by sonication and next generation sequencing","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hrthm.2022.01.039","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Disclosures: Dr Nielsen received a grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF16OC0018658 ). All other authors have reported that they have no relationships relevant to the contents of this paper to disclose. Funding sources: This work was supported by the Danish Heart Association and the Region of Southern Denmark (15-R99-A5950-22895, 16/36792)."],"id":"S02-098.86-014039","identifier":[{"id":"85125932103","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35124230","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-13f49424-1c05-428b-be77-ad3d4e5da468","sdu-011613c1-e930-41f7-b63b-460d982f1103"],"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device","Cardiac implantable electronic device infection","Defibrillators, Implantable/adverse effects","Device-related infection","Electronics","Heart Diseases","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Infection","Molecular microbiology","Next-generation sequencing","Pacemaker, Artificial/adverse effects","Prosthesis-Related Infections/diagnosis","Sonication","Sonication/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-7FA3A9DC5C2FE2E113A4BFA2762C1970"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335421263/Microbiological_diagnosis_in_cardiac_implantable_electronic_device_infections_detected_by_sonication_and_next_generation_sequencing.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202926070/PIIS154752712200114X.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hrthm.2022.01.039","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Un