{"abstract":"We performed a randomised, blinded, controlled study with adult patients scheduled for primary total knee arthroplasty under spinal anaesthesia. The aim was to investigate the analgesic effects of adductor canal block using catheter-based repeated boluses, either through a new suture-method catheter or a standard perineural catheter, compared with a single-injection technique. All patients received an adductor canal block after surgery with an initial bolus of 20 ml ropivacaine 0.75%, followed by 20 ml of ropivacaine 0.2% every 8 h in the standard and suture-method catheter groups, and sham boluses for the single-injection group. The primary outcome measure was total opioid consumption (intravenous morphine equivalents) from the end of surgery until 12:00 on postoperative day 2. Secondary outcomes were pain, muscle strength and ambulation. We randomly assigned (1:1:1) and analysed 153 patients. Total opioid consumption was median (IQR [range]) 24 (11–37 [0–148]) mg in the suture-method group, 38 (17–51 [0–123]) mg in the standard catheter group and 37 (14–57 [0–158]) mg in the single-injection group (p = 0.049). Differences were not statistically significant after Bonferroni correction (α = 0.05/3). There were no differences between groups on postoperative day 1. On postoperative day 2, there were no differences between catheter groups, but muscle strength and ambulation were improved compared with the single-injection group. We conclude that providing repeated boluses via a catheter did not decrease opioid consumption or pain compared with a single injection, but improved muscle strength and ambulation on postoperative day 2. The two types of catheters were similar.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lyngeraa, T. S.","Jæger, P.","Gottschau, B.","Graungaard, B.","Rossen-Jørgensen, A. M.","Toftegaard, I.","Grevstad, Jens Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459978"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Regional anaesthesia","Total knee replacement","femoral nerve block","saphenous nerve block"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of the analgesic effect of an adductor canal block using a new suture method catheter vs standard perineural catheter vs single injection a randomised blinded controlled study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-459978","identifier":[{"id":"85071308369","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31465115","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6f5e5bfd-5074-4adc-bd05-e632a2199f02"],"keyword":["femoral nerve block","regional anaesthesia","saphenous nerve block","total knee replacement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF837AE5874732DB0370E1BB0C67BB7C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"T. S.","key":"lyngeraapau","last":"Lyngeraa","name":"Lyngeraa, T. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"P.","key":"jægerpau","last":"Jæger","name":"Jæger, P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B.","key":"gottschaupau","last":"Gottschau","name":"Gottschau, B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B.","key":"graungaardpau","last":"Graungaard","name":"Graungaard, B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A. M.","key":"rossenjørgensenpau","last":"Rossen-Jørgensen","name":"Rossen-Jørgensen, A. M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"I.","key":"toftegaardpau","last":"Toftegaard","name":"Toftegaard, I.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"U.","key":"grevstadpau","last":"Grevstad","locid":"05545c66-a842-40eb-8a4c-d1efc910553a","name":"Grevstad, Jens Ulrik","name_org":"Grevstad, U.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31465115"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/anae.14814","issn":["00032409","13652044"],"issn_org":["00032409"],"issue":"11","journal":"Anaesthesia","pages":"1397-1405","status":"p","title":"Anaesthesia","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071308369"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6f5e5bfd-5074-4adc-bd05-e632a2199f02"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparison of the analgesic effect of an adductor canal block using a new suture-method catheter vs. standard perineural catheter vs. single-injection : a randomised, blinded, controlled study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-459978","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","Werenberg, Helene","Rosholm, Jens-Ulrik","Herrstedt, Jørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640741"],"event":{"end":"2019-09-27","place":"Krakow, pl","start":"2019-09-25","title":"15th EuGMS Congress","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of polypharmacy and potential inappropriate medication with toxicity to anti neoplastic treatment","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-640741","ids":["sdu-ebc06221-deae-4543-8b26-686d15d7ec82"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-486A9EAA8EA8B2E3CAE8203E2E4E5C4B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Lembrecht","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"f9eac821-ade9-44b6-8f42-747089a921cf","name":"Jørgensen, Trine Lembrecht","orcid":"0000-0002-7968-2694","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"werenbergpau","last":"Werenberg","locid":"f6bc4419-b23d-4025-968b-bfd64b64c8e3","name":"Werenberg, Helene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens-Ulrik","key":"rosholmpau","last":"Rosholm","locid":"42011e4d-4ddc-4850-bf2b-1fba8b412125","name":"Rosholm, Jens-Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0003-4730-467X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn","key":"herrstedtpau","last":"Herrstedt","locid":"ea88fcb8-e0ec-4439-815d-d3ead82a2a7c","name":"Herrstedt, Jørn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ebc06221-deae-4543-8b26-686d15d7ec82"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Polypharmacy and Potential Inappropriate Medication with Toxicity to Anti-Neoplastic Treatment","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640741","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The majority of young women use oral contraceptives (OCs). Use of OCs has been associated with lower myofibrillar protein and tendon collagen synthesis rates, but it is unknown whether OCs will limit the adaptive response of myotendinous tissue to resistance training. Design and Methods: Fourteen healthy untrained young regular OC users (24 ± 1 years, fat% 32 ± 1, 35 ± 2 ml⋅min-1⋅kg-1) and 14 NOC users (non-OC, controls) (24 ± 1 years, fat% 32 ± 2, 34 ± 2 ml⋅min-1⋅kg-1) performed a 10-week supervised lower extremity progressive resistance training program. Before and after the intervention biopsies from the vastus lateralis muscle and the patellar tendon were obtained. Muscle (quadriceps) and tendon cross-sectional area (CSA) was determined by magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scans, and muscle fiber CSA was determined by histochemistry. Maximal isometric knee extension strength was assessed by dynamometry while 1 repetition maximum (RM) was determined during knee extension. Results: Training enhanced CSA in both muscle (p < 0.001) and tendon (p < 0.01). A trend toward a greater increase in muscle CSA was observed for OC (11%) compared to NOC (8%) (interaction p = 0.06). Analysis of mean muscle fiber type CSA showed a trend toward an increase in type II muscle fiber area in both groups (p = 0.11, interaction p = 0.98), whereas type I muscle fiber CSA increased in the OC group (n = 9, 3821 ± 197 to 4490 ± 313 mm2, p < 0.05), but not in NOC (n = 7, 4020 ± 348 to 3777 ± 354 mm2, p = 0.40) (interaction p < 0.05). Post hoc analyses indicated that the effect of OCs on muscle mass increase was induced by the OC-users (n = 7), who used OCs containing 30 μg ethinyl estradiol (EE), whereas the response in users taking OCs with 20 μg EE (n = 7) did not differ from NOC. Both the OC and NOC group experienced an increase in maximal knee strength (p < 0.001) and 1RM leg extension (p < 0.001) after the training period with no difference between groups. Conclusion: Use of OCs during a 10-week supervised progressive resistance training program was associated with a trend toward a greater increase in muscle mass and a significantly greater increase in type I muscle fiber area compared to controls. Yet, use of OCs did not influence the overall increase in muscle strength related to training.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Jensen, Line","Dalgas, Ulrik","Andersen, Jesper L","Rossen, Niklas B","Møller, Andreas Buch","Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Hans","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","Kovanen, Vuokko","Couppé, Christian","Langberg, Henning","Kjær, Michael","Hansen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-088.03-029118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Eastern Finland"],"keyword":["Biomechanical properties","Estradiol","Estrogen","Exercise","In vivo","Mechanical properties","Menstrual Cycle","Muscle Strength","Muscle hypertrophy","Protein synthesis","Skeletal muscle","Tendon","Women"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of oral contraceptive use on adaptations to resistance training","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphys.2019.00824","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by grants from the NIH (R01 HL-084487 to AE and R01 GM-111397 to JR-F)."],"id":"S02-088.03-029118","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6614284","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85077298115","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31312144","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000473687500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85089242029","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e2e72eb4-905c-453f-90e8-e1dda16a6b37","ku-e0cba309-2262-4bf7-8524-cf5aaa8c1246"],"keyword":["BIOMECHANICAL PROPERTIES","HUMAN ACHILLES-TENDON","IN-VIVO","MECHANICAL-PROPERTIES","MENSTRUAL-CYCLE","MUSCLE-FIBER SIZE","PROTEIN-SYNTHESIS","SKELETAL-MUSCLE","TENDON COLLAGEN-SYNTHESIS","TESTOSTERONE LEVELS","estradiol","estrogen","exercise","muscle hypertrophy","muscle strength","tendon","women"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-733609841C27AAC0CB6DC1F41F7AB89B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/225381161/Influence_of_Oral_Contraceptive_Use_on_Adaptations_to_Resistance_Training.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6614284/pdf/fphys-10-00824.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphys.2019.00824","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Sport Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg og Frederiksberg Universitets Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"university of eastern finland","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Eastern Finland","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line B","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"e136f41f-f605-4357-a0fb-258e8f7a10fc","name":"Jensen, Line","name_org":"Dalgaard, Line B","orcid":"0000-0001-7676-5323","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik","key":"dalgaspau","last":"Dalgas","locid":"2102ffe9-e66f-4d73-b757-78b5630fb6d6","name":"Dalgas, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0003-4132-2789","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Jesper L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicklas B","key":"rossenpau","last":"Rossen","locid":"fde04f7b-b73f-42bb-8fed-7ced5a87b6fc","name":"Rossen, Niklas B","name_org":"Rossen, Nicklas B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Buch","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"6a97bc2c-14c1-484b-b439-bc90d5406d20","name":"Møller, Andreas Buch","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas Buch","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","name":"Moller, Andreas Buch","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"stødkildejørgensenpau","last":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen","locid":"5d4cd2e1-37e5-468a-9048-d492c0a466bf","name":"Stødkilde-Jørgensen, Hans","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans","key":"stodkildejorgensenpau","last":"Stodkilde-Jorgensen","name":"Stodkilde-Jorgensen, Hans","rank"