{"abstract":"\"Treatment of antipsychotic-associated obesity with a GLP-1 receptor agonist (GLP-1RA): The TAO trial\" is the first clinical investigation of GLP-1RA treatment (exenatide 2 mg once-weekly or placebo) in antipsychotic-treated schizophrenia patients with obesity.1 Recently, we published the main results from the TAO trial as an original article in Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism.2 We regret to report, that further analyses of the TAO dataset have revealed an error in our secondary analyses presented in the original publication.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ebdrup, Bjørn H","Broberg, Brian V","Ishøy, Pelle L","Bak, Nikolaj","Andersen, Ulrik B","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Holst, Jens J","Knop, Filip K","Glenthøj, Birte Y"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580312"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Letter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"erratum to effect of glp 000000000001 receptor agonist treatment on body weight in obese antipsychotic treated patients with schizophrenia a randomized placebo controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/135019050/Erratum_to_Effect_of_GLP_1_receptor_agonist_treatment_on_body_weight_in_obese_antipsychotic_treated_patients_with_schizophrenia_a_randomized_placebo_controlled_trial.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580312","identifier":[{"id":"85040861178","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6885958","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29316175","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-18b771cb-6549-4720-a8cb-6fe01f89a91c"],"keyword":["Letter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAFA418AAE10BC34290D045C9B2155ED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/135019050/Erratum_to_Effect_of_GLP_1_receptor_agonist_treatment_on_body_weight_in_obese_antipsychotic_treated_patients_with_schizophrenia_a_randomized_placebo_controlled_trial.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn H","key":"ebdruppau","last":"Ebdrup","name":"Ebdrup, Bjørn H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian V","key":"brobergpau","last":"Broberg","name":"Broberg, Brian V","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pelle L","key":"ishøypau","last":"Ishøy","name":"Ishøy, Pelle L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","name":"Bak, Nikolaj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik B","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ulrik B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niklas R","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"cc73de9e-169b-4cd1-8e1c-1a2c3827b3e8","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jørgensen, Niklas R","orcid":"0000-0001-9624-5210","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Jens J","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Filip K","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","name":"Knop, Filip K","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Birte Y","key":"glenthøjpau","last":"Glenthøj","name":"Glenthøj, Birte Y","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29316175"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/dom.13204","issn":["14628902","14631326"],"issn_org":["14628902"],"issue":"5","journal":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","pages":"1327-1328","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040861178"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-18b771cb-6549-4720-a8cb-6fe01f89a91c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Erratum to : Effect of GLP-1 receptor agonist treatment on body weight in obese antipsychotic-treated patients with schizophrenia: a randomized, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580312","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The optimal timing of invasive coronary angiography (ICA) and revascularization in patients with non-ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome is not well defined. We tested the hypothesis that a strategy of very early ICA and possible revascularization within 12 hours of diagnosis is superior to an invasive strategy performed within 48 to 72 hours in terms of clinical outcomes. METHODS: Patients admitted with clinical suspicion of non-ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome in the Capital Region of Copenhagen, Denmark, were screened for inclusion in the VERDICT trial (Very Early Versus Deferred Invasive Evaluation Using Computerized Tomography) ( ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02061891). Patients with ECG changes indicating new ischemia or elevated troponin, in whom ICA was clinically indicated and deemed logistically feasible within 12 hours, were randomized 1:1 to ICA within 12 hours or standard invasive care within 48 to 72 hours. The primary end point was a combination of all-cause death, nonfatal recurrent myocardial infarction, hospital admission for refractory myocardial ischemia, or hospital admission for heart failure. RESULTS: A total of 2147 patients were randomized; 1075 patients allocated to very early invasive evaluation had ICA performed at a median of 4.7 hours after randomization, whereas 1072 patients assigned to standard invasive care had ICA performed 61.6 hours after randomization. Among patients with significant coronary artery disease identified by ICA, coronary revascularization was performed in 88.4% (very early ICA) and 83.1% (standard invasive care). Within a median follow-up time of 4.3 (interquartile range, 4.1-4.4) years, the primary end point occurred in 296 (27.5%) of participants in the very early ICA group and 316 (29.5%) in the standard care group (hazard ratio, 0.92; 95% CI, 0.78-1.08). Among patients with a GRACE risk score (Global Registry of Acute Coronary Events) >140, a very early invasive treatment strategy improved the primary outcome compared with the standard invasive treatment (hazard ratio, 0.81; 95% CI, 0.67-1.01; P value for interaction=0.023). CONCLUSIONS: A strategy of very early invasive coronary evaluation does not improve overall long-term clinical outcome compared with an invasive strategy conducted within 2 to 3 days in patients with non-ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome. However, in patients with the highest risk, very early invasive therapy improves long-term outcomes. CLINICAL TRIAL REGISTRATION: URL: https://www.clinicaltrials.gov . Unique identifier: NCT02061891.","author_count":48,"contributors":["Kofoed, Klaus F","Kelbæk, Henning","Hansen, Peter Riis","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Høfsten, Dan","Kløvgaard, Lene","Holmvang, Lene","Helqvist, Steffen","Jørgensen, Erik","Galatius, Søren","Pedersen, Frants","Bang, Lia","Saunamaki, Kari","Clemmensen, Peter","Linde, Jesper J","Heitmann, Merete","Wendelboe Nielsen, Olav","Raymond, Ilan E","Kristiansen, Ole Peter","Svendsen, Ida Hastrup","Bech, Jan","Dominguez Vall-Lamora, Maria Helena","Kragelund, Charlotte","Hansen, Thomas Fritz","Dahlgaard Hove, Jens","Jørgensen, Tem","Fornitz, Gitte G","Steffensen, Rolf","Jurlander, Birgit","Abdulla, Jawdat","Lyngbæk, Stig","Elming, Hanne","Therkelsen, Susette Krohn","Abildgaard, Ulrik","Jensen, Jan Skov","Gislason, Gunnar","Køber, Lars V","Engstrøm, Thomas"],"cuid":["S03-093.99-010838"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Kofoed, Klaus F."],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome diagnosis","Acute coronary syndrome","Aged","Clinical outcome","Coronary Angiography methods","Coronary revascularization","Female","Heart Arrest etiology","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","PCI","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome","Troponin metabolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Depts. of Rheumatology and Radiology, Musculoskeletal Statistics Unit, Hospitals of Slagelse, Graasten, Gentofte, Aarhus, Frederiksberg, Silkeborg, Hjørring, Odense, Herlev, the Parker Institute and Rigshospitalet, Zealand, Funen and Jutland, Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early versus standard care invasive examination and treatment of patients with non st segment elevation acute coronary syndrome verdict randomized controlled trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85058892770&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was funded by the Danish Agency for Science, Technology, and Innovation and the Danish Council for Strategic Research (grant no. 09–066994) and the Research Council of Rigshopitalet. None of the funding bodies has taken any part in study design, study conduct, or data analysis and has had no role in writing the article. Dr Kofoed reports grants from the Danish Research Foundation during the conduct of the study, in addition to grants from the Research Council of Rigshospi-talet, AP Møller og hustru Chastine McKinney Møllers Fond, the Danish Heart Foundation, and Canon Medical Corporation outside the submitted work. Dr Kober reports grants from the Danish Research Foundation during the conduct of the study. Dr Torp-Pedersen reports grants from Bayer outside the submitted work. Dr Linde reports grants from the Danish Research Foundation and the Research Council of Rigshospitalet during the conduct of the study. Dr Abdulla reports personal fees from Novartis Healthcare outside the submitted work. Dr Engstrøm reports personal fees from Abbott, Astra Zeneca, Bayer, Boston Scientific, and Novo outside the submitted work. The other authors report no conflicts of interest."],"id":"S03-093.99-010838","identifier":[{"id":"85058892770","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30565996","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e2eeb64e-d092-42df-9887-eb75cb3a99f6","ku-a26cd091-1b85-48b7-a94a-936a46df6ff2","sdu-1100e26a-b08a-4db4-97fb-53b666b21402"],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome/diagnosis","Aged","Coronary Angiography/methods","Female","Heart Arrest/etiology","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","PCI","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention/adverse effects","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors","Treatment Outcome","Troponin/metabolism","acute coronary syndrome","clinical outcome","coronary revascularization","time factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4D6DD3A23EF487B33591CEDFEC1B9033"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university",