{"abstract":"Dopamine plays a key role in the cellular and behavioral responses to drugs of abuse, but the implication of metabotropic regulatory input to dopaminergic neurons on acute drug effects and subsequent drug-related behavior remains unclear. Here, we used chemogenetics [Designer Receptors Exclusively Activated by Designer Drugs (DREADDs)] to modulate dopamine signaling and activity before cocaine administration in mice. We show that chemogenetic inhibition of dopaminergic ventral tegmental area (VTA) neurons differentially affects locomotor and reward-related behavioral responses to cocaine. Stimulation of Gi-coupled DREADD (hM4Di) expressed in dopaminergic VTA neurons persistently reduced the locomotor response to repeated cocaine injections. An attenuated locomotor response was seen even when a dual-viral vector approach was used to restrict hM4Di expression to dopaminergic VTA neurons projecting to the nucleus accumbens. Surprisingly, despite the attenuated locomotor response, hM4Di-mediated inhibition of dopaminergic VTA neurons did not prevent cocaine sensitization, and the inhibitory effect of hM4Di-mediated inhibition was eliminated after withdrawal. In the conditioned place-preference paradigm, hM4Di-mediated inhibition did not affect cocaine-induced place preference; however, the extinction period was extended. Also, hM4Di-mediated inhibition had no effect on preference for a sugar-based reward over water but impaired motivation to work for the same reward in a touchscreen-based motivational assay. In addition, to support that VTA dopaminergic neurons operate as regulators of reward motivation toward both sugar and cocaine, our data suggest that repeated cocaine exposure leads to adaptations in the VTA that surmount the ability of Gi-signaling to suppress and regulate VTA dopaminergic neuronal activity.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Runegaard, Annika H","Sørensen, Andreas Toft","Fitzpatrick, Ciarán M","Jørgensen, Søren H.","Petersen, Anders Victor","Hansen, Nikolaj Winther","Weikop, Pia","Andreasen T., Jesper","Mikkelsen, Jens D","Perrier, Jean-Francois Marie","Woldbye, David Paul Drucker","Rickhag, Mattias","Wortwein, Gitta","Gether, Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-428874"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"locomotor and reward enhancing effects of cocaine are differentially regulated by chemogenetic stimulation of gi signaling in dopaminergic neurons","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/ENEURO.0345-17.2018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-428874","identifier":[{"id":"29938215","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6011418","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85052159139","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3b5ea150-ff30-4673-aded-873317260c39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9A6CA66C0ACCDF422187F8867A0DC1B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209056989/Locomotor_and_Reward_Enhancing_Effects_of_Cocaine_Are_Differentially_Regulated_by_Chemogenetic_Stimulation_of_Gi_Signaling_in_Dopaminergic_Neurons.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/ENEURO.0345-17.2018","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Neuropharm and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services Glostrup"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Annika H","key":"runegaardpau","last":"Runegaard","locid":"64b18da7-bb62-442d-9378-e5fabfed2630","name":"Runegaard, Annika H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas T","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ac0f6a72-7014-4f0c-8c02-6c9a7721ccbd","name":"Sørensen, Andreas Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Andreas T","orcid":"0000-0001-5887-9247","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ciarán M","key":"fitzpatrickpau","last":"Fitzpatrick","locid":"882de932-ff04-42a8-828b-a361baa48114","name":"Fitzpatrick, Ciarán M","orcid":"0000-0002-9996-4541","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren H","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"062ac31a-9b01-439e-a82e-5fb49b108a99","name":"Jørgensen, Søren H.","name_org":"Jørgensen, Søren H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders V","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"567799a9-aaef-4a71-a998-f766c955426f","name":"Petersen, Anders Victor","name_org":"Petersen, Anders V","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nikolaj W","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"af7e6d22-82f8-4c69-b23a-7a6951c06425","name":"Hansen, Nikolaj Winther","name_org":"Hansen, Nikolaj W","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"weikoppau","last":"Weikop","locid":"03dfc781-ac58-469d-a16a-12067a22f8fc","name":"Weikop, Pia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper T","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"bc66d36f-6969-4fa0-9b43-ac503a438a8a","name":"Andreasen T., Jesper","name_org":"Andreasen, Jesper T","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens D","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"4ee068c8-9463-4ec9-a19d-800376e1badb","name":"Mikkelsen, Jens D","orcid":"0000-0002-0498-6861","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jean-Francois","key":"perrierpau","last":"Perrier","locid":"71b8f851-db1f-4222-89be-5a20d8ac9c1c","name":"Perrier, Jean-Francois Marie","name_org":"Perrier, Jean-Francois","orcid":"0000-0002-9189-3574","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"woldbyepau","last":"Woldbye","locid":"bc523287-caff-4eb5-932c-990fa1e1ac90","name":"Woldbye, David Paul Drucker","name_org":"Woldbye, David","orcid":"0000-0002-6321-3850","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mattias","key":"rickhagpau","last":"Rickhag","locid":"b5357d5f-af02-4476-bdff-b0625852e352","name":"Rickhag, Mattias","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gitta","key":"wortweinpau","last":"Wortwein","name":"Wortwein, Gitta","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrik","key":"getherpau","last":"Gether","locid":"9b3eed37-e0b0-412a-b790-48069d4d1e5e","name":"Gether, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-0020-3807","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29938215"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1523/eneuro.0345-17.2018","issn":["23732822"],"issue":"3","journal":"eNeuro","paperid":"e0345","status":"p","title":"eNeuro","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052159139"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3b5ea150-ff30-4673-aded-873317260c39"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Locomotor- and Reward-Enhancing Effects of Cocaine Are Differentially Regulated by Chemogenetic Stimulation of Gi-Signaling in Dopaminergic Neurons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-428874","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: There are limited data to guide the optimum approach to patients presenting with angina after coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG). Although often referred for invasive angiography, the effectiveness of this is unknown; angina may also result from diffuse distal or micro-vascular coronary disease and it is not known how often targets for intervention are identified. METHODS: Retrospective review of 50,460 patients undergoing angiography in East Denmark between January 2010 and December 2014. Clinical and procedural data were prospectively stored in a regional electronic database. Follow-up data were available for all patients, by means of records linked to each Danish social security number. RESULTS: In patients with prior CABG and stable angina (n = 2,309), diagnostic angiography led to revascularization in 574 (24.9%) cases. Chronic kidney disease (HR 1.93 [1.08-3.44], P = 0.027), significant angina (HR 1.49 [1.18-1.88], P = 0.006 for angina class ≥ II, and HR 2.04 [1.61-2.58], P < 0.001 for angina class ≥ III) and a positive pre-procedural stress test (HR 2.56 [1.42-4.60], P < 0.001) were independent predictors of revascularization. Stress testing was, however, used less frequently than in patients without prior CABG (17.2% vs. 24.2%, P < 0.001). The positive predictive values for subsequent revascularization were 47.8%, 51.4%, and 66.9% for exercise ECG, stress echocardiography, and myocardial perfusion scintigraphy (MPS), respectively. CONCLUSIONS: Invasive angiography leads to revascularization in a quarter of patients with angina and prior CABG; the threshold for referral may be too low. Non-invasive stress testing predicts the need for revascularization but appears underused and MPS, in particular, may better identify patients likely to require revascularization. © 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Joshi, Francis R","Biasco, Luigi","Pedersen, Frants","Holmvang, Lene","Helqvist, Steffen","Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","Abildgaard, Ulrik","Kelbaek, Henning","Lassen, Jens F","Jørgensen, Erik","De Backer, Ole","Engstrøm, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-529663"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Angina Stable diagnostic imaging","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Bypass adverse effects","Denmark","Echocardiography Stress","Electrocardiography","Exercise Test","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Predictive Value of Tests","Referral and Consultation","Registries","Retreatment","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"invasive angiography and revascularization in patients with stable angina following prior coronary artery bypass grafting results from the east denmark heart registry","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-529663","identifier":[{"id":"85013288112","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27219901","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e42c6d0c-0dc3-4036-a219-ce6a43eccf54"],"keyword":["Aged","Angina, Stable/diagnostic imaging","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Bypass/adverse effects","Denmark","Echocardiography, Stress","Electrocardiography","Exercise Test","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Perfusion Imaging","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention","Predictive Value of Tests","Referral and Consultation","Registries","Retreatment","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6D7BF8CCBBBE080900B7ED742C2A0610"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Francis R","key":"joshipau","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Francis R","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Luigi","key":"biascopau","last":"Biasco","name":"Biasco, Luigi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Frants","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Frants","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","locid":"54b8ef01-f8ed-4c49-a126-2109e2fd351f","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steffen","key":"helqvistpau","last":"Helqvist","name":"Helqvist, Steffen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans-Henrik","key":"tilstedpau","last":"Tilsted","name":"Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik","key":"abildgaardpau","last":"Abildgaard","name":"Abildgaard, Ulrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henning","key":"kelbaekpau","last":"Kelbaek","name":"Kelbaek, Henning","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens F","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","name":"Lassen, Jens F","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Erik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ole","key":"debackerpau","last":"De Backer","name":"De Backer, Ole","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"engstrømpau","last":"Engstrøm","locid":"77ddb69e-092a-4c53-bbf0-409cdd3d12f7","name":"Engstrøm, Thomas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27219901"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ccd.26598","issn":["15221946","1522726X"],"issn_org":["15221946"],"issue":"3","journal":"Catheterization and Cardiovascular Interventions","pages":"341-349","status":"p","title":"Catheterization and Cardiovascular Interventions","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013288112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e42c6d0c-0dc3-4036-a219-ce6a43eccf54"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Invasive angiography and revascularization in patients with stable angina following prior coronary artery bypass grafting : Results from the East Denmark heart registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-529663","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The article discusses transition dynamics towards a Danish low-carbon society based on studies of energy production and consumption. This article shows how the Arena of Development and policy mix approaches may inform the analysis of system transition to a low carbon society. The Arena of Development approach is an actor-centred approach that focuses on how path dependencies of socio-technical systems may be challenged when controversies and matters-of-concern produce ‘arenas’ where established governance configurations and policies of a socio-technical system are challenged. Re-organising actor-constellations are constitutional for arenas and define their boundaries and the policies employed. We discuss the historic transitions in relation to four focal areas of Danish attempts to become independent of fossil energy: wind-power integration in the energy system, energy savings, biomass and sustainable mobility. The analysis demonstrates the conflicts and mixes of policy measures that have moved transition processes forward, but sometimes also stalling them. The analysis shows how changing controversies, arena configurations and policy mixes move forward the energy transition process.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Michael Søgaard","Jørgensen, Ulrik","Jensen, Jens Stissing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-062684"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Energy transition","Matters of concern","Policy mixes","arena of development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"navigations and governance in the danish energy transition reflecting changing arenas of development controversies and policy mixes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-062684","identifier":[{"id":"000415942100016","type":"wos"},{"id":"85034710011","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2b9eefdb-a7a9-4390-984f-b5da6481faa0"],"keyword":["Energy transition","Matters of concern","Policy mixes","arena of development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B3B7EC0CA2E3E3E154BC32AE6ED40B7"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Center for Design, Innovation and Sustainable Transitions","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, SUSTAINABLE DESIGN AND TRANSITION"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Søgaard","key":"jørgensenmichaelsøgaardpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d06cf6e7-16ad-49e7-8f8d-9b3bf7bff9f9","name":"Jørgensen, Michael Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6646-7250","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik","key":"jørgensenulrikpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"1f0bc31d-a06f-44ad-a068-b38866fff6fb","name":"Jørgensen, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8863-1418","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Stissing","key":"jensenjensstissingpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"75cb3a27-7322-4fe9-bbf3-c815190a05bf","name":"Jensen, Jens Stissing","orcid":"0000-0003-3535-3773","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.erss.2017.09.034","issn":["22146296"],"journal":"Energy Research and Social Science","pages":"173-185","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy Research and Social Science","title_org":"Energy Research & Social Science","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034710011"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2b9eefdb-a7a9-4390-984f-b5da6481faa0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Navigations and governance in the Danish energy transition reflecting changing Arenas of Development, controversies and policy mixes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-062684","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Ayres, Phil","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Jørgensen, Jens Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-127779"],"event":{"end":"2017-12-03","place":"København, dk","start":"2017-09-07","title":"Cirkulær økonomi i arkitektur og design","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adaptive architecture","Plants","Robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-127779","ids":["arkc-a62943db-4c04-452a-bf6f-9b5306225eb9"],"keyword":["No","adaptive architecture","braided structures","growing architecture","plants","robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-465FD90E0D44D43C1BFBE2A6739DD02D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayresoth","last":"Ayres","locid":"809e3672-ddc8-44e7-8a1b-1c1309974305","name":"Ayres, Phil","orcid":"0000-0002-9266-065X","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichoth","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ulrik","key":"jørgensenppu","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"b9ff6d25-9d86-4621-b5c7-ac3dba0cc077","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Ulrik","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-a62943db-4c04-452a-bf6f-9b5306225eb9"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Flora Robotica","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-127779","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Schizophrenia is associated with cardiovascular co-morbidity and a reduced life-expectancy of up to 20 years. Antipsychotics are dopamine D2 receptor antagonists and the standard of medical care in schizophrenia, but the drugs are associated with severe metabolic side effects like obesity and diabetes. Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1RAs) are registered for treatment of both obesity and type 2 diabetes. We investigated metabolic effects of the GLP-1RA, exenatide once-weekly, in non-diabetic, antipsychotic-treated, obese patients with schizophrenia. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Antipsychotic-treated, obese, non-diabetic, schizophrenia spectrum patients were randomized to double-blinded adjunctive treatment with once-weekly subcutaneous exenatide (n = 23) or placebo (n = 22) injections for three months. The primary outcome was body weight loss after treatment and repeated measures analysis of variance was used as statistical analysis. RESULTS: Between March 2013 and June 2015, 40 patients completed the trial. At baseline, the mean body weight was 118.3 ± 16.0 kg in the exenatide group and 111.7 ± 18.0 kg in the placebo group, with no group differences (P = 0.23). The exenatide and placebo groups experienced significant (P = 0.004), however, similar (P = 0.98) weight losses of 2.24 ± 3.3 kg and 2.23 ± 4.4 kg, respectively, after three months of treatment. CONCLUSIONS: Treatment with exenatide once-weekly did not promote weight loss in obese, antipsychotic-treated patients with schizophrenia compared to placebo. Our results could suggest that the body weight-lowering effect of GLP-1RAs involves dopaminergic signaling, but blockade of other receptor systems may also play a role. Nevertheless, anti-obesity regimens effective in the general population may not be readily implemented in antipsychotic-treated patients with schizophrenia ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT01794429.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ishøy, Pelle L","Knop, Filip K.","Broberg, Brian V","Bak, Nikolaj","Andersen, Ulrik B","Jørgensen, Niklas R","Holst, Jens Juul","Glenthøj, Birte","Ebdrup, Bjørn H."],"cuid":["S02-098.85-043779"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of glp 000000000001 receptor agonist treatment on body weight in obese antipsychotic treated patients with schizophrenia a randomized placebo controlled trial byline","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/dom.12795","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.85-043779","identifier":[{"id":"27717222","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5299524","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85006371317","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7d3ee1fc-d1c4-4aeb-a54e-aa9f03b1909d","sdu-a8089bf8-32e7-4354-8de8-ea8d4900b11d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-32704D0E4FDD85944CC11B5641C0F653"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/180789043/Ish_y_et_al_2016_Diabetes_Obesity_and_Metabolism.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5299524/pdf/DOM-19-162.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124380494/Effect_of_GLP_1_receptor_agonist_treatment_on_body_weight_in_obese_antipsychotic_treated_patients_with_schizophrenia.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/dom.12795","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Pelle L","key":"ishøypau","last":"Ishøy","name":"Ishøy, Pelle L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Filip K","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Filip K","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Brian V","key":"brobergpau","last":"Broberg","name":"Broberg, Brian V","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolaj","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","name":"Bak, Nikolaj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"