{"abstract":"Reverse Electro-Enhanced Dialysis (REED) has been shown to intensify fermentations which are impaired by an ionic product inhibition. Productivity can be greatly enhanced by the in situ product removal from the cultivation broth. The REED process has been tested for different applications, where its strong potential for increasing productivity and product yield has been verified. REED uses ion exchange membranes and electrical potential gradients to selectively separate the target ion. The main limitation of using membrane separation combined with bioreactors is membrane fouling. REED technology ensures long operation time by reversing periodically the polarity of the imposed electrical field to significantly reduce the influence of membrane fouling. The periodic nature of the electrically driven membrane separation process makes the membrane bioreactor operation non trivial. This challenging operation is associated with different dynamic behaviors of the individual units plus their interaction. The purpose of this contribution is to show the results of experimental and model based efforts done in order to investigate the operation of a membrane bioreactor. From modeling point of view, it is interesting to reveal to which extend the REED module can facilitate the pH control in the fermenter. In this case, the membrane and reactor unit interactions are exploited to substantially increase the lactate productivity and substrate utilization compared to a conventional fermentation with a crude control of pH. Experiments using multiple stacks with asynchronical current reversal intervals for improved pH stability were carried out in a bioreactor connected to a REED system. The REED was used for control of the pH process parameter of the bioreactor through exchanging the lactate ions (from lactic acid produced in the bioreactor) with hydroxide ions, which maintained a pH close to optimal growing conditions. The ion-exchange was in turn regulated by a PID control unit, which adjusted the electrical current output between the REED electrodes to match the growing production speed of lactic acid, which increased during the trials as the LAB culture grew in numbers simultaneously. For the single stack trial, the fluctuations deviate significantly more from the setpoint, compared to the similar setup with multiple stacks operated with dispersed, asyncronical current reversal intervals. For the single stack, no other effect helps to stabilize the pH fluctuations until the current reversal transition has passed and process parameter control is reassessed to bring back the pH to its setpoint. For multiple stacks, the operating stacks immediately respond to the impact of one stack going into current reversal and increase their effect while the single stack recovers. Thereby the deviations are significantly lower, which is preferable, especially when operating with microbial process liquids or continuous process solutions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Prado Rubio, Oscar Andres","Garde, Arvid","Rype, Jens-Ulrik","Jørgensen, Sten Bay","Jonsson, Gunnar Eigil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354643"],"event":{"end":"2012-11-08","place":"Aachen, de","start":"2012-11-07","title":"14th Aachener Membrane Kolloquium","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing inhibited fermentations through a dynamic electro membrane bioreactor","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-354643","ids":["dtu-a7d6629f-a844-4d58-bc12-1dae40cf8068"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E6C982644ADF24CDDC6372E1A4B4AC76"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Computer Aided Process Engineering Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oscar Andres","key":"pradorubiopau","last":"Prado Rubio","locid":"34ba9671-5725-4ffe-909c-d6e98ae39d9f","name":"Prado Rubio, Oscar Andres","orcid":"0000-0003-1419-542X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arvid","key":"gardepau","last":"Garde","locid":"6880491c-edf6-47e1-bdab-eda336498275","name":"Garde, Arvid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens-Ulrik","key":"rypepau","last":"Rype","locid":"b4766e79-2630-4998-a852-d31205461ba3","name":"Rype, Jens-Ulrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten Bay","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"748f61d0-3828-4a27-8f91-6ba0937eb514","name":"Jørgensen, Sten Bay","orcid":"0000-0002-3179-972X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunnar Eigil","key":"jonssonpau","last":"Jonsson","locid":"3cad998b-6169-4b60-8976-ed4af90ee63c","name":"Jonsson, Gunnar Eigil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a7d6629f-a844-4d58-bc12-1dae40cf8068"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Enhancing inhibited fermentations through a dynamic electro-membrane bioreactor","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354643","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Aims. We evaluated the feasibility, safety and efficacy of intra-myocardial injection of autologous mesenchymal stromal cells derived endothelial progenitor cell (MSC) in patients with stable coronary artery disease (CAD) and refractory angina in this first in man trial. Methods and results. A total of 31 patients with stable CAD, moderate to severe angina and no further revascularization options, were included. Bone marrow MSC were isolated and culture expanded for 6-8 weeks. It was feasible and safe to establish in-hospital culture expansion of autologous MSC and perform intra-myocardial injection of MSC. After six months follow-up myocardial perfusion was unaltered, but the patients increased exercise capacity (p <0.001), reduction in CCS Class (p <0.001), angina attacks (p <0.001) and nitroglycerin consumption (p <0.001), and improved Seattle Angina Questionnaire (SAQ) evaluations (p <0.001). For all parameters there was a tendency towards improved outcome with increasing numbers of cells injected. In the MRI substudy: ejection fraction (p <0.001), systolic wall thickness (p = 0.03) and wall thickening (p = 0.03) all improved. Conclusions. The study demonstrated that it was safe to treat patients with stable CAD with autologous culture expanded MSC. Moreover, MSC treated patients had significant improvement in left ventricular function and exercise capacity, in addition to an improvement in clinical symptoms and SAQ evaluations.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Friis, Tina","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Mathiasen, Anders Bruun","Ripa, Rasmus S","Kristoffersen, Ulrik Sloth","Jørgensen, Erik","Hansen, Louise","Bindslev, Lene","Kjaer, Andreas","Hesse, Birger","Dickmeiss, Ebbe","Kastrup, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446008"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mesenchymal stromal cell derived endothelial progenitor treatment in patients with refractory angina","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14017431.2011.569571","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446008","identifier":[{"id":"79957523072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-57eb6fb9-60b9-4cd0-9569-5227e11df690"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24ACB894851B062C7B9C6D5C46C0B5E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/14017431.2011.569571","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Tina","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Tina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mandana","key":"haacksørensenpau","last":"Haack-Sørensen","name":"Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders B","key":"mathiasenpau","last":"Mathiasen","locid":"9dda0e1c-af26-43e0-8ba6-3de29980b77e","name":"Mathiasen, Anders Bruun","name_org":"Mathiasen, Anders B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus S","key":"ripapau","last":"Ripa","name":"Ripa, Rasmus S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik S","key":"kristoffersenpau","last":"Kristoffersen","locid":"0feeab5a-3bd6-4dac-8ea4-fdc4de0cbd85","name":"Kristoffersen, Ulrik Sloth","name_org":"Kristoffersen, Ulrik S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"224b751a-5dbe-4a53-ac9b-7461e8face39","name":"Jørgensen, Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Louise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","name":"Bindslev, Lene","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birger","key":"hessepau","last":"Hesse","locid":"ee337e17-5641-456b-b0f6-183d6b8672f4","name":"Hesse, Birger","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ebbe","key":"dickmeisspau","last":"Dickmeiss","locid":"3737db7a-dba7-4e16-ba6d-73a840ceb9c6","name":"Dickmeiss, Ebbe","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"kastruppau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"12c1241f-23da-492c-84b0-36691cb95255","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/14017431.2011.569571","issn":["14017431"],"issue":"3","journal":"Scandinavian Cardiovascular Journal","pages":"161-8","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Cardiovascular Journal","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79957523072"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-57eb6fb9-60b9-4cd0-9569-5227e11df690"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mesenchymal stromal cell derived endothelial progenitor treatment in patients with refractory angina","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446008","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The exhalant jet flow of mussels in conjunction with currents and/or other mussels may strongly influence the mussels' grazing impact. Literature values of mussel exhalant jet velocity vary considerably and the detailed fluid mechanics of the near-mussel flow generated by the exhalant jet has hitherto been uncertain. Computational modelling of this phenomenon depends on knowledge of the velocity distribution near the exhalant siphon aperture of mussels to provide appropriate boundary conditions for numerical flow models. To be useful such information should be available for a range of mussel shell lengths. Here, we present results of a detailed study of fully open mussels Mytilus edulis in terms of filtration rate, exhalant siphon aperture area, jet velocity, gill area and body dry weight, all as a function of shell length (mean +/- SD) over the range 16.0 +/- 0.4 to 82.6 +/- 2.9 mm, with the corresponding scaling laws also presented. The exhalant jet velocity was determined by 3 methods: (1) measured clearance rate divided by exhalant aperture area, (2) manual particle tracking velocimetry (PTV) using video-microscope recordings, and (3) particle image velocimetry (PIV). The latter provides detailed 2-component velocity distributions near the exhalant siphon in 5 planes parallel to the axis of the jet and the major axis of the oval aperture, and hence estimates of momentum and kinetic energy flows in addition to mean velocity. Data obtained on particles inside the exhalant jet of filtered water was verified by the use of titanium dioxide seeding particles which were de-agglomerated by ultrasound to a size range of 0.7 to 2 mu m prior to addition, to avoid retention by the gill filter of the mussels. We found that exhalant jet velocity was essentially constant at similar to 8 cm s(-1), and independent of shell length. Based on geometric similarity and scaling of mussel pump-system characteristics we found that these characteristics coincide approximately for all sizes when expressed as pressure head versus volume flow divided by shell length squared.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Riisgard, Hans Ulrik","Jørgensen, Bo Hoffmann","Lundgreen, Kim","Storti, Francesca","Walther, Jens Honore","Meyer, Knud Erik","Larsen, Poul S."],"cuid":["S02-093.65-036851"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Filtration rate","Particle image velocimetry","Particle tracking velocimetry","Velocity field"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the exhalant jet of mussels mytilus edulis","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3354/meps09268","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.65-036851","identifier":[{"id":"80052876572","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bc14ce7d-1488-4d50-ac6f-fe930124c1b2","sdu-c9071eb9-566f-494a-86df-88b35958e808"],"keyword":["Allometric equation","Exhalant jet velocity","Exhalant siphon area","Filtration rate","Particle image velocimetry","Particle tracking velocimetry","Scaling law","Velocity field"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1EC13374CCD2186A499BCDD993FE5488"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3354/meps09268","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5877701/F366Dd01.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Ulrik","key":"riisgårdpau","last":"Riisgård","locid":"c985ce16-a6f2-45d6-a499-37dc1e77fb96","name":"Riisgård, Hans Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8188-2951","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo Hoffmann","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"f915db17-db79-42c7-904d-eca033549257","name":"Jørgensen, Bo Hoffmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"hoffamannpau","last":"Hoffamann","name":"Hoffamann, Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim","key":"lundgreenpau","last":"Lundgreen","locid":"16b9cdbb-4ca7-49f9-a17d-26b492d4682c","name":"Lundgreen, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-201X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"stortipau","last":"Storti","locid":"533aa91e-a0d8-44ab-a950-073119b53e11","name":"Storti, Francesca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Honore","key":"waltherpau","last":"Walther","locid":"9895a63e-6fff-429b-8188-9bcd7f6cac8d","name":"Walther, Jens Honore","orcid":"0000-0001-8100-9178","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud Erik","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"42818c4a-ed99-4819-a1ae-919f718fc73f","name":"Meyer, Knud Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-2179-0235","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":